    {
      "id": 20,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Changing the config",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 34
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Grafana can't publish MQTT, so config is changed with a **retained** message on the broker (`mqtt.leetserve.com`). Every field is optional; the device echoes what it accepted to `config/applied` (table above, `errors` column).\n\n```sh\n# switch mode / widen a band / slow the sample rate\nmosquitto_pub -h mqtt.leetserve.com -r -t grow/tent1/config -m '{\n  \"mode\": \"flower\",\n  \"sample_interval_s\": 30,\n  \"targets\": { \"flower\": { \"temp\": [20, 26], \"rh\": [45, 55], \"vpd\": [1.1, 1.4], \"co2\": [] } }\n}'\n# quick mode change only\nmosquitto_pub -h mqtt.leetserve.com -r -t grow/tent1/mode -m veg\n```\n\nFields: `mode` (veg/flower/dry/cure), `leaf_offset_c` (-10..10), `sample_interval_s` (2..60, **clears on-device history**), `screen_timeout_s` (0 = never), `window` (10m/1h/6h/1d/3d/1w), `enable_co2`, `targets.<mode>.<temp|rh|vpd|co2>` = `[lo, hi]` or `[]` to remove. Full reference: github.com/gabeduke/wio-grow-monitor."
      }
    }
